{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrvs9sgQePSchKr2yvfi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause is in `reporting/dedupe.py`: `seen_ids` is a list, so each `event_id in seen_ids` check is a linear scan, making dedupe O(n²). At 30k rows that is roughly 450 million string comparisons. The refactor switched from a set to a list, which is why the output stays correct. I'll switch the membership check back to a set and keep the list for insertion order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10437,"cache_read_input_tokens":26884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10437},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89d15f9c-7856-4fcf-b879-7abfb420b718","uuid":"95dfe537-8897-4fe0-9c22-9628b80189c2","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:50:55.752Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrvs9e2oki1X6NGG71rn"}
