{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrvu1CbP8KHwZPjsMw2j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause was in `reporting/dedupe.py`. The refactor changed the duplicate check from a set to a list, so every `event_id in seen_ids` scanned the whole list. That made dedupe quadratic, and the nightly report slowed down with it.\n\n**Fix:** `dedupe_rows` now tracks seen IDs in a set and still appends to the output list, so first-occurrence order is preserved. The output and public API are unchanged.\n\n**Measurement** (30k unique rows plus 5k duplicates):\n- Before: 4.85 s\n- After: 0.006 s\n- Output identical to the old version.\n\n**Regression test:** `tests/test_dedupe.py` adds two tests:\n- `test_dedupe_keeps_first_occurrence_in_order` checks ordering and first-wins behaviour on a small input.\n- `test_dedupe_large_input_is_not_quadratic` runs 35k rows and asserts the result is correct and the run takes under 1 s. I checked that it fails against the old list-based code (5.86 s, 1 failed) and passes with the fix.\n\n**Full suite:** `python3 -m pytest` reports 3 passed.\n\nI did not commit. The changes are in the working tree: `reporting/dedupe.py` modified, `tests/test_dedupe.py` new."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3421,"cache_read_input_tokens":46270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3421},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89d15f9c-7856-4fcf-b879-7abfb420b718","uuid":"2002d2b4-1aad-4d6a-b85f-4d68d0b07a01","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:51:21.708Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvtztVJUN3JJD1NRUpr"}
